//
// A MASKED LOCAL STORED NARROW IS REFUSED (`@FR-N-Arith`, `@FR-N-Store`).  The range `x & 255`
// proves is asked at the store that meets the mask; a local bound to it is an `integer`, its range
// is its declaration, so `m = x & 255; lo: u8 = m` narrows a value nothing proves fits (owner
// ruling 2026-10-19: an implicitly narrowed local type would surprise its reader).  The cures the
// diagnostic names — the mask at the store, `?? <value>`, a `u8?` destination — all compile.
//
// @falsified-at: 3cae84177 — interpret and native: the store compiles (the local carried
//   `limit(0, 255)`).
// CHANNEL: the expected diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the source as `integer` and the destination `u8`.
// HOLDS: the mask at the store compiles (the sibling cell).
// @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot implicitly narrow integer to u8

fn main() {
  x = 1000;
  m = x & 255;
  lo: u8 = m;
  println("{lo}");
}
